cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ColorFrame, please cite it as below. Implementation by AI development agents under the author's direction; see docs/AI_USAGE.md."
title: "ColorFrame: frame-aware candidate path search in coloured sequence graphs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mohammadi
    given-names: Ali
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AliMohammadiiii/ColorFrame"
abstract: >-
  A controlled algorithmic and engineering prototype that enumerates forward-strand ORFs along
  walks of small coloured sequence graphs under strict and permissive sample-support policies,
  implemented in Python, C++17 and Rust with byte-identical outputs. Not a gene caller.
keywords: [coloured de Bruijn graph, open reading frame, graph traversal, benchmarking]
